To create a Custom REST Service in Dynamics AX using X++, you can follow the below steps:

Step 1: Create a new class by navigating to the Class node in the AOT and right-clicking to select New Class. Name the class CustomRESTService.

Step 2: Add the following code to the class to create a custom REST service:

```x++
class CustomRESTService
{
    [SysEntryPointAttribute(true)]
    public void processGetRequest()
    {
        System.NullPointerException nullPointerException;
        System.IO.StringWriter stringWriter;

        try
        {
            container jsonContainer;

            //Logic to process GET request
            jsonContainer = yourLogicHere();

            str response = this.serializeToJson(jsonContainer);

            SysHttpResponseHelper::setJsonResponse(SysHttpResponseStatusCode::Ok, 'application/json', response);
        }
        catch (exception::Error)
        {
            throw error(strFmt("An error occurred while processing the GET request."));
        }
        catch (exception::Warning)
        {
            throw error(strFmt("A warning occurred while processing the GET request."));
        }
        catch (exception::Info)
        {
            throw error(strFmt("An informative message occurred while processing the GET request."));
        }
        catch
        {
            throw error(strFmt("An unknown error occurred while processing the GET request."));
        }
    }

    //Helper method to serialize container to JSON
    private str serializeToJson(container _container)
    {
        System.Json.Stringify(_container);
    }
}
```

Step 3: Now, deploy the customization to your Dynamics AX environment. To do this, right-click on the project containing your class and select Deploy to deploy the changes.

Step 4: Finally, you can test your custom REST service by sending a GET request to the service endpoint. The endpoint will be something like https://<yourDynamicsAXEnvironment>/api/services/CustomRESTService/processGetRequest.

